+# Agent Note: Session-owned details preferences
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-06-session-details-preferences.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A global details preference makes selecting one Session apply another Session’s open state, maximization and ordinary width. Reloading cannot restore visibility when persistence excludes it.
+
+## Decision
+
+The [layout store](../../../../packages/client/ui-layout/src/client/stores.ts) owns one persisted map keyed by branded SessionId. The frame derives the selected entry without copying it into current-layout fields. Service gestures resolve the current Session at invocation; drag callbacks retain their starting Session and ignore a changed selection. The no-Session landing has no writable entry. Closing preserves width and maximization.
+
+The storage key is `dsh.layout.panels.v2`. Unattributed global preferences under `dsh.layout.panels.v1` are ignored rather than assigned to every Session.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Global preferences** cannot express independent layouts. **A current-layout mirror plus a Session map** requires save/restore ordering during selection and can write stale values into the target Session. Direct projection keeps one authority.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Selection and browser refresh restore each Session’s visibility, maximization and ordinary width. Frame column subtrees retain their mounted positions. Preferences remain browser-local, and deleted Sessions are not pruned from this map. The [AppFrame tests](../../../../packages/client/ui-layout/tests/app-frame.client.spec.tsx) cover selection, refresh, no-Session defaults and delayed drag isolation; real managed-browser activation remains an integration verification step.
